Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 12:01:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 108/154] feat(profiles): choose the window a profile's data
 link opens in
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The choice is a pure function over candidates in activation order, so it is a
unit test with fakes rather than a browser: the first window on that profile
that is realised and not little wins, and no match asks for a new one.

Two of those conditions come from real failures. A tab added to a Browser with
no native window aborts the process, and a little window is chromeless and
single-tab, so a settings page has nowhere to go.

The live scan and the new-window fallback are a thin adapter over it, left for
the browsertest that lands with the routes.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
index c3d3121b25cec..5803d5005a170 100644
